-**Theorem** (natural-number weights, read as probabilities where valid; two stages, four plans, and a chance drawn afresh at each stage or once; near-definitional, with witnesses). *When complying when read and acting by its own law when not is best.* A formation read at one stage and not at a later one complies or acts by its own law at each (`ReadStages.Act`, `ReadStages.Plan`). Its prospects are a total `T`; the weights `k_C` and `k_O` of its law's being kept after it complies when read and after it acts by its own law then; the value `V` of acting by its law at the unread stage where kept; and the loss `c` of complying when read (`ReadStages.Prospects`). Read as probabilities they ask a positive total and each weight within it (`ReadStages.Prospects.Valid`); a plan's gain and loss are the two parts of its expected value times the total, and one plan stands above another where its gain with the other's loss exceeds the other's gain with its loss (`ReadStages.Prospects.Above`). Complying when read and acting by its own law when not stands above every other plan exactly where `k_O V + c T < k_C V`, which in probabilities is the weight complying adds to being kept, times the value, strictly exceeding the loss (`ReadStages.Prospects.KeepingOutweighs`, `ReadStages.complyThenOwn_best_iff`); acting by its own law at both does exactly where `k_O V` is positive and `k_C V < k_O V + c T` (`ReadStages.ownAtBoth_best_iff`); and no other plan ever does, complying at the unread stage never standing above acting by its own law after the same act (`ReadStages.unread_comply_not_above`). Every maximal plan, one nothing stands above, is complying when read and acting by its own law when not exactly where keeping outweighs the loss (`ReadStages.Prospects.Maximal`, `ReadStages.only_complyThenOwn_iff`), and the choice taking that plan there and acting by its own law at both otherwise, ties included, is maximal (`ReadStages.choose_optimal`, `ReadStages.choose_eq_iff`, `ReadStages.choose_of_not_outweighs`). Keeping outweighs the loss only with a value at the unread stage and complying raising the weight of being kept and, with that weight within the total, only where the value exceeds the loss (`ReadStages.outweighs_needs`, `ReadStages.outweighs_needs_more`); with either absent, the first two exits, the choice is acting by its own law at both, which with `0 < c T` stands above the plan and with no loss can tie with it (`ReadStages.no_value_chooses_own`, `ReadStages.kept_not_raised_chooses_own`, `ReadStages.ownAtBoth_above_without_value`, `ReadStages.ownAtBoth_above_of_not_raised`, `ReadStages.Example.exit_tie`). With the stages as `Bool`, `true` the read stage, a plan is open to some act law reading them through a lumping exactly where the plan has one act at both stages or the lumping tells the stages apart (`ReadStages.plan_realized_iff`, by `Learning.Lumped`), so complying when read and acting by its own law when not is open exactly there (`ReadStages.complyThenOwn_realized_iff`), and for such a law a lumping tying the stages is the third exit. Where the lumping tells them apart, by [what readings fix of the unread](#r-what-readings-fix-of-the-unread) at the two stages, every selection through agreement on the read stage that selects a law reading through the lumping and complying when read also selects one reading through it that takes the plan (`ReadStages.twin_complyThenOwn`); where it ties them, by [generalization through lumping](#r-generalization-through-lumping), the read stage fixes the act at the unread one (`ReadStages.read_fixes_unread`), and among plans with one act at both stages acting by its own law at both stands above the other where `k_O V + c T` is positive (`ReadStages.uniform_best_iff`). A law that cannot tell the stages apart but draws its act afresh at each stage, each draw independent of the other, complying with chance `m / (m + r)` for `0 < m`, stands above acting by its own law at both exactly where `(m + r) (k_O V + c T) + r k_O V < r k_C V` (`ReadStages.Prospects.FreshDrawAbove`, `ReadStages.freshDraw_above_iff_chance`), so for some chance exactly where `2 k_O V + c T < k_C V` (`ReadStages.freshDraw_above_iff`): not telling the stages apart raises the threshold by `k_O V`, which can be nothing, and leaves complying with some chance at each stage able to stand above acting by its own law at both, while the first two exits hold against such a law (`ReadStages.freshDraw_not_above_without_value`, `ReadStages.freshDraw_not_above_of_not_raised`) and a single draw between the two uniform plans never stands above it (`ReadStages.Prospects.MixtureAbove`, `ReadStages.mixture_never_above`). In a witness with valid prospects the plan is uniquely best and chosen, and complying with chance one in eight or one in five at each stage stands above acting by its own law at both, the best uniform plan there, while one in four does not (`ReadStages.Example.valid`, `ReadStages.Example.best`, `ReadStages.Example.chosen`, `ReadStages.Example.freshDraw_above`, `ReadStages.Example.freshDraw_boundary`) ([record](../results/records/when-complying-when-read-is-best.md)).
